  "phase3_gemini_self_healing": {
    "forensics": "Three of the five losing trades (ITC, TATASTEEL #4, ICICIBANK) were entered during the mid-day or late-afternoon sessions (11:25 to 14:10) and failed to reach the ambitious 1.45% target before the EOD square-off, turning minor price stagnation and a gross-positive trade (TATASTEEL #4) into net losses due to severe fee drag (\u20b937.14 total fees vs \u20b95.90 net P&L). The remaining two losses (INFY, TATASTEEL #3) both triggered at 10:25 AM and suffered stop-loss whipsaws right around the 0.65% threshold during post-opening range consolidation.",
    "learning": "In Indian NSE large-cap cash equities, intraday volatility decays rapidly after 11:00 AM; demanding a high 1.45% target without exceptional volume conviction leads to EOD time-decay exits where statutory brokerage and STT charges erode gross profitability.",
